/*
  protocol/blake_calc_stressable.spthy -- PROTOCOL LAYER, Blake's CALC_SK posed as 'Hard'.
  The opt-in counterpart of protocol/blake_calc.spthy: it ONLY poses the request and leaves the
  answer to the core masks (core/masks/attentive_calc.spthy, busy_calc.spthy, ...), exactly as
  Alex's request/ack variant (protocol/msg3_request.spthy) does for Alex.

  Posing CALC_SK as 'Hard' lets the sigma1 trigger (core/stressors/cognitive_load.spthy, which
  reads !Req(P,...,'Hard')) fire for Blake and emit SetMask('Blake','Busy'); the core busy_calc
  then answers as Busy and slips. Because the answer is the SHARED core mask (keyed on party P),
  Blake reuses the same human layer as Alex -- no Blake-specific mask file. An experiment that uses
  this file does NOT include ceremony.base.spthy (which carries the Easy default); it assembles
  types + init + messages + this file directly (see 18_blake_busy_calc.spthy).
*/

rule B_pose_calc_hard:
    [ BlakeWait(idB, <Na,Nb>), Fr(~rid) ]
  --[ Request('Blake', ~rid, 'CALC_SK', 'Hard') ]->
    [ !Req('Blake', ~rid, 'CALC_SK', <Na,Nb>, 'Hard'),
      // Layer-1 objective step for the agnostic interface (sigma3 reads 'compute' + lexicon).
      !Step('Blake', ~rid, 'compute') ]
